.TH BOSWAS-WINAPP 1 "October 2026" "boswas-compat 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-winapp \- install and run Windows applications in isolated sandboxes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-winapp
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-winapp
is the Boswas OS compatibility tool for Windows applications. Every
application gets its own Wine prefix, runs inside its own bubblewrap sandbox,
and is confined by the
.B boswas-winapp
AppArmor profile. Windows software is never run as root.
.PP
An application can access only its own prefix, plus whatever its
compatibility manifest (or, for unlisted installers, the device policy) grants:
network, display, audio, GPU, and selected folders such as Documents.
The user's home directory, other applications, the session D-Bus and raw
devices are never visible.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "install " INSTALLER " [\-\-id " ID "] [\-\-name " NAME "] [\-\-portable] [\-\-interactive] [\-\-timeout " S "] [\-\-verbose] [\-\- " ARGS ]
Verify the installer (.exe or .msi), match it against the compatibility
catalog by SHA-256 (or by
.BR \-\-id ),
create the application's prefix and run the installer in the sandbox.
Silent switches are used when the manifest names them or the installer
framework is recognised;
.B \-\-interactive
shows the installer's own dialogs.
.B \-\-portable
copies a self-contained program instead of running it.
.TP
.BI "inspect " INSTALLER " [\-\-id " ID "] [\-\-name " NAME "] [\-\-portable]"
Check an installer without installing anything: file type, Windows
architecture, catalog match, sandbox and the policy decision. Exits 0 if the
installer would be accepted and 4 if it would be refused. Nothing is run.
.TP
.BI "upgrade " "APPLICATION INSTALLER" " [\-\-interactive] [\-\-timeout " S "] [\-\-verbose] [\-\- " ARGS ]
Run a newer installer of an installed application in its existing prefix,
keeping its data. A catalogued application accepts only the installer its
manifest pins.
.TP
.BI "remove " APPLICATION
Remove the application, its prefix and its desktop entry.
.TP
.BI "stop " APPLICATION
Stop a running application: its sandbox and every Windows process in it end
(like "End task"; unsaved work is lost).
.TP
.B runtime
Show the Windows compatibility runtime: Wine, the supported architectures
(x86_64 only), bubblewrap, the AppArmor profile mode and the policy in effect.
Exits 1 if it is not healthy.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fB\-\-all\-users\fR]
List installed applications. With
.B \-\-all\-users
(root only) list every user's applications for device inventory.
.TP
.BI "launch " APPLICATION " [\-\-exe " PROGRAM "] [\-\-timeout " S "] [\-\-quiet] [\-\- " ARGS ]
Start the application in its sandbox. Its output is shown and logged.
.TP
.BI "status " APPLICATION
Show state, catalog status, policy decision, sandbox grants and the
AppArmor confinement of the last launch.
.TP
.BI "repair " APPLICATION
Update the prefix, re-apply the Boswas prefix defaults and the desktop entry,
and verify the program still exists.
.TP
.BI "logs " APPLICATION " [\-\-install | \-\-repair | \-\-launch | \-\-clear] [\-\-lines " N ]
Show the latest launch log (or, if there is none, the latest log of any
kind), the latest install, repair or launch log, or delete the
application's logs.
.TP
.B catalog
List the compatibility catalog and the effective policy.
.TP
.BI "manifest validate " FILE ...
Validate compatibility manifests.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/boswas/wine/<id>/
Application data: record, logs, and the sandbox state (prefix and private
home) that appears as
.I /var/lib/boswas/wine/<id>/
inside the sandbox.
.TP
.I /etc/boswas/compat/policy.conf
Device policy (root).
.TP
.I /var/lib/boswas/compat/policy.conf
Managed device policy, written by the Boswas device agent from a verified,
signed Control Plane policy; used instead of the local policy when present.
.TP
.I /var/lib/boswas/compat/manifests/
Managed compatibility catalog (Control Plane).
.TP
.IR /usr/share/boswas/compat/manifests/ ", " /etc/boswas/compat/manifests/
System and local compatibility catalogs.
.TP
.I /etc/apparmor.d/boswas-winapp
AppArmor profile; local additions in
.IR /etc/apparmor.d/local/boswas-winapp .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 operation failed; 2 usage error; 3 not found; 4 refused by
policy or a safety rule; 5 runtime or confinement unavailable; 6 busy;
70 internal error. After a program has started,
.B launch
returns the program's exit code.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas (1),
.BR bwrap (1),
.BR apparmor (7),
.BR wine (1)
